        <ArticleTitle>[Comparative animal experiments of bile duct anastomoses using microsurgical technics].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>244-53</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>The purpose of the study was to optimize the microsurgical technique of the choledochus anastomosis and fibrin glue adhesion by long-term experiments with rats. By comparing clinical, laboratory-chemical, radiological and histological characteristics of 5 test-groups with a control group 6 months after performing the operations the microsurgical interrupted suture of the obliquely interrupted choledochus showed the best results. Because there is a tendency of post operative stenosis the fibrin glue adhesion could not be recommended.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
